    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21HmhWYod2RaAgEd2pLGd8h)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent: based on `main`, no dependencies.\n- Touches `sp-org-base` (doc and `.el`), the `sp-org-lint` doc and `global-keymap-namespaces.org`; one line of code only.\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks.\n- Branch name is not number-prefixed (cloud sessions cannot rename it); rename by hand if you want it.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Key chosen: `C-x t I`** (Shift-i), in `org-mode-map`, runs `sp-org-lint-resources`.\n- Why this key:\n  - `org-toggle-item` is `C-x t i` in `sp-org-base`; the lint turns stray lines into items with that command.\n  - Same prefix, shifted letter: easy to remember.\n- Clash check:\n  - the `tab-bar` prefix `C-x t` has no uppercase `I`\n  - no other binding of `C-x t I` in the config\n  - no CUA keys (`C-z/c/x/v`), no leader (`C-;`), no Alfred or input-source keys involved\n  - GUI-only keymap, as agreed\n- Docs (bullet lists):\n  - `sp-org-base.org`: keybinding list and code block\n  - `sp-org-lint.org`: replaces \"no key bindings are set\"\n  - `global-keymap-namespaces.org`: `C-x t i/h/d/I` merge with the tab prefix\n- Not run: `tools/check-tangle.sh` (no Emacs in the container); the `.el` line is the same text as the doc block. `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] In an Org buffer, select a messy list of links, press `C-x t I`: blank lines and duplicates removed, sorted alphabetically\n- [ ] `C-h k C-x t I` shows `sp-org-lint-resources`\n- [ ] `C-x t i` still toggles an item, and `C-x t h`, `C-x t d` still work\n- [ ] Outside Org, `C-x t` tab commands still work (e.g. `C-x t 2`)\n- [ ] One `C-/` undo reverts the whole lint\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAy7Xo1sNaJXggvTp7)_",
